     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"crown:obtain is an OR, so both h4_0:pivot and h4_1:access must be made unreachable. h4_1:access is an OR over h2_0, h3_1 and h3_0. h2_0:traverse is reachable directly from the entry footholds, and h3_0:access is reachable through h1_0, which is an OR of the footholds. No single block below h4_1 can cut all three of these routes, so h4_1 itself must be blocked. Blocking h4_1 does not affect h4_0:pivot, which is still reachable through its own parents, so it needs at least one more block. Blocking h3_0:access (or h4_0 directly) breaks that AND. This gives a minimum of 2, for example {h4_1:access, h3_0:access}.\"}"
    }
